3133}, {"text": "the Multiple Choice Answer Sheet", "x0": 0.1054945054945055, "y0": 0.13442113442113443, "x1": 0.3879120879120879, "y1": 0.14763014763014762}, {"text": "Waves are a disturbance that carries", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.16783216783216784, "x1": 0.4230769230769231, "y1": 0.17793317793317792}, {"text": "1.", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.11868131868131868, "y1": 0.17871017871017872}, {"text": "a) matter", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.19968919968919968, "x1": 0.24395604395604395, "y1": 0.21212121212121213}, {"text": "b) energy", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.21522921522921523, "x1": 0.24615384615384617, "y1": 0.22843822843822845}, {"text": "\u00a9) particles", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.23076923076923078, "x1": 0.25934065934065936, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "and matter", "x0": 0.25164835164835164, "y0": 0.2463092463092463, "x1": 0.33406593406593404, "y1": 0.2564102564102564}, {"text": "The transverse progressive wave shown below has a frequency of 0.1 hertz.", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.27583527583527584, "x1": 0.7274725274725274, "y1": 0.2898212898212898}, {"text": "Sy", "x0": 0.2703296703296703, "y0": 0.2975912975912976, "x1": 0.2824175824175824, "y1": 0.30691530691530694}, {"text": "wave movement", "x0": 0.421978021978022, "y0": 0.32400932400932403, "x1": 0.5087912087912088, "y1": 0.32944832944832947}, {"text": "S", "x0": 0.3505494505494505, "y0": 0.4149184149184149, "x1": 0.3626373626373626, "y1": 0.425019425019425}, {"text": "\u2018What is the time in seconds for the crest at surfer S; to move to the surfer at $;?", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.43045843045843046, "x1": 0.7615384615384615, "y1": 0.4428904428904429}, {"text": "a) 10", "x0": 0.14835164835164835, "y0": 0.46386946386946387, "x1": 0.21428571428571427, "y1": 0.47707847707847706}, {"text": "b) 5", "x0": 0.14835164835164835, "y0": 0.4801864801864802, "x1": 0.20549450549450549, "y1": 0.4926184926184926}, {"text": "15", "x0": 0.1989010989010989, "y0": 0.494949494949495, "x1": 0.21428571428571427, "y1": 0.5050505050505051}, {"text": "d 3", "x0": 0.14945054945054945, "y0": 0.5104895104895105, "x1": 0.20549450549450549, "y1": 0.5236985236985237}, {"text": "When a wave enters a more dense medium it bends:", "x0": 0.14945054945054945, "y0": 0.54001554001554, "x1": 0.5494505494505495, "y1": 0.5516705516705517}, {"text": "a) away from the normal", "x0": 0.14945054945054945, "y0": 0.5710955710955711, "x1": 0.37032967032967035, "y1": 0.585081585081585}, {"text": "b) parallel to the normal", "x0": 0.14945054945054945, "y0": 0.5866355866355867, "x1": 0.3648351648351648, "y1": 0.6006216006216006}, {"text": "\u00a9) the normal", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6021756021756022, "x1": 0.34945054945054943, "y1": 0.6161616161616161}, {"text": "4) parallel to the boundary between the two media", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.616938616938617, "x1": 0.567032967032967, "y1": 0.6317016317016317}, {"text": "For light travelling from air to glass the refractive index is 1.5.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6480186480186481, "x1": 0.6329670329670329, "y1": 0.6627816627816627}, {"text": "The critical angle of incidence for this piece of glass would be", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.6635586635586636, "x1": 0.6329670329670329, "y1": 0.6775446775446775}, {"text": "a) 30\u00b0", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6954156954156954, "x1": 0.22527472527472528, "y1": 0.7101787101787101}, {"text": "b) 90\u00b0", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.710955710955711, "x1": 0.22527472527472528, "y1": 0.7249417249417249}, {"text": "42\u00b0", "x0": 0.2, "y0": 0.7264957264957265, "x1": 0.22527472527472528, "y1": 0.7373737373737373}, {"text": "d 52\u00b0", "x0": 0.15274725274725276, "y0": 0.7420357420357421, "x1": 0.22527472527472528, "y1": 0.756021756021756}, {"text": "Which of the following circuit components will not increase the resistance of the circuit?", "x0": 0.15274725274725276, "y0": 0.7707847707847708, "x1": 0.8384615384615385, "y1": 0.7863247863247863}, {"text": "a) Increasing the length of the conductor", "x0": 0.15384615384615385, "y0": 0.7956487956487956, "x1": 0.4956043956043956, "y1": 0.822066822066822}, {"text": "b) the temperature of the conductor", "x0": 0.15274725274725276, "y0": 0.818958818958819, "x1": 0.5395604395604395, "y1": 0.8337218337218337}, {"text": "Changing the conductor to one of greater resistance", "x0": 0.2021978021978022, "y0": 0.8344988344988346, "x1": 0.6010989010989011, "y1": 0.8484848484848485}, {"text": "4) Increasing the cross sectional area of the conductor", "x0": 0.15384615384615385, "y0": 0.8422688422688422, "x1": 0.5978021978021978, "y1": 0.8679098679098679}], [{"text": "\u2018The question refers to the following diagram:", "x0": 0.13736263736263737, "y0": 0.06060606060606061, "x1": 0.4846153846153846, "y1": 0.07459207459207459}, {"text": "6.", "x0": 0.1, "y0": 0.06216006216006216, "x1": 0.11208791208791209, "y1": 0.07226107226107226}, {"text": "V Volts", "x0": 0.46373626373626375, "y0": 0.07303807303807304, "x1": 0.5384615384615384, "y1": 0.1048951048951049}, {"text": "a", "x0": 0.3824175824175824, "y0": 0.09168609168609168, "x1": 0.42747252747252745, "y1": 0.12354312354312354}, {"text": "Ry ohms", "x0": 0.17802197802197803, "y0": 0.2261072261072261, "x1": 0.26483516483516484, "y1": 0.2540792540792541}, {"text": "Switch -", "x0": 0.321978021978022, "y0": 0.2494172494172494, "x1": 0.42857142857142855, "y1": 0.2634032634032634}, {"text": "\u2018When the switch is closed, the potential difference across resistor Re will be", "x0": 0.14065934065934066, "y0": 0.2773892773892774, "x1": 0.7263736263736263, "y1": 0.29215229215229216}, {"text": "YR, volts", "x0": 0.1934065934065934, "y0": 0.3123543123543124, "x1": 0.26153846153846155, "y1": 0.32944832944832947}, {"text": "4) R+R,", "x0": 0.14175824175824175, "y0": 0.32556332556332557, "x1": 0.24835164835164836, "y1": 0.3457653457653458}, {"text": "tk,", "x0": 0.210989010989011, "y0": 0.34654234654234656, "x1": 0.2549450549450549, "y1": 0.35275835275835277}, {"text": "b)", "x0": 0.14175824175824175, "y0": 0.37373737373737376, "x1": 0.15714285714285714, "y1": 0.3861693861693862}, {"text": "VR, volts", "x0": 0.1945054945054945, "y0": 0.40559440559440557, "x1": 0.26043956043956046, "y1": 0.4156954156954157}, {"text": "\u2014_", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.4133644133644134, "x1": 0.26263736263736265, "y1": 0.43045843045843046}, {"text": "R+R", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.4289044289044289, "x1": 0.24835164835164836, "y1": 0.4382284382284382}, {"text": "itt", "x0": 0.210989010989011, "y0": 0.439005439005439, "x1": 0.2549450549450549, "y1": 0.44522144522144524}, {"text": "VR, volts", "x0": 0.1956043956043956, "y0": 0.466977466977467, "x1": 0.26373626373626374, "y1": 0.47707847707847706}, {"text": "ad 2", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.47785547785547783, "x1": 0.2230769230769231, "y1": 0.49184149184149184}, {"text": "R", "x0": 0.22087912087912087, "y0": 0.4902874902874903, "x1": 0.23296703296703297, "y1": 0.4996114996114996}, {"text": "Lighting in suburban homes is wired up in", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.526029526029526, "x1": 0.4703296703296703, "y1": 0.54001554001554}, {"text": "a) parallel configurations", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.5578865578865578, "x1": 0.367032967032967, "y1": 0.5710955710955711}, {"text": "b) series circuits", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.5734265734265734, "x1": 0.2978021978021978, "y1": 0.5866355866355867}, {"text": "\u00a9) separate circuits for each light", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.5881895881895882, "x1": 0.42527472527472526, "y1": 0.6021756021756022}, {"text": "4) two lights only per circuit", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.6045066045066045, "x1": 0.3934065934065934, "y1": 0.6177156177156177}, {"text": "A ship sails 10km due north then 15km due west.", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.6348096348096348, "x1": 0.5252747252747253, "y1": 0.6480186480186481}, {"text": "The magnitude and direction of its displacement from its starting point is closest to:", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.6487956487956488, "x1": 0.7901098901098901, "y1": 0.6635586635586636}, {"text": "a) 35kmNW", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.6822066822066822, "x1": 0.27362637362637365, "y1": 0.6954156954156954}, {"text": "b) 50\u00b0 W", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.6907536907536908, "x1": 0.3120879120879121, "y1": 0.714063714063714}, {"text": "c) 35kmN 50\u00b0E", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.7047397047397047, "x1": 0.3065934065934066, "y1": 0.7311577311577312}, {"text": "\u2018An object initially at rest is dropped from a height of 100m.", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.7591297591297591, "x1": 0.6054945054945055, "y1": 0.7731157731157731}, {"text": "When it is 25m from the ground, the ratio of its kinetic energy to its potential energy is", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.7738927738927739, "x1": 0.8175824175824176, "y1": 0.7878787878787878}, {"text": "2", "x0": 0.14835164835164835, "y0": 0.8383838383838383, "x1": 0.16263736263736264, "y1": 0.8508158508158508}], [{"text": ". When a cricket player catches a ball he draws his hands back on impact when the ball reaches", "x0": 0.13736263736263737, "y0": 0.07692307692307693, "x1": 0.8747252747252747, "y1": 0.09867909867909867}, {"text": "his hands. This reduces the", "x0": 0.15494505494505495, "y0": 0.09246309246309246, "x1": 0.3637362637362637, "y1": 0.10567210567210568}, {"text": "a) impulse", "x0": 0.15384615384615385, "y0": 0.12432012432012432, "x1": 0.26263736263736265, "y1": 0.13752913752913754}, {"text": "b) time", "x0": 0.15274725274725276, "y0": 0.13986013986013987, "x1": 0.23516483516483516, "y1": 0.1522921522921523}, {"text": "\u00a2) momentum change", "x0": 0.15274725274725276, "y0": 0.1554001554001554, "x1": 0.34945054945054943, "y1": 0.17094017094017094}, {"text": "@) force", "x0": 0.15274725274725276, "y0": 0.17094017094017094, "x1": 0.23956043956043957, "y1": 0.18337218337218336}, {"text": "+ Elastic collisions involve conservation of", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.20279720279720279, "x1": 0.4725274725274725, "y1": 0.21678321678321677}, {"text": "a) momentum only", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.2338772338772339, "x1": 0.3263736263736264, "y1": 0.24864024864024864}, {"text": "b) momentum but not kinetic energy", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.2494172494172494, "x1": 0.46153846153846156, "y1": 0.26573426573426573}, {"text": "c) momentum and kinetic energy", "x0": 0.15054945054945054, "y0": 0.26495726495726496, "x1": 0.4340659340659341, "y1": 0.2812742812742813}, {"text": "@) kinetic energy only", "x0": 0.14945054945054945, "y0": 0.2804972804972805, "x1": 0.34725274725274724, "y1": 0.29526029526029524}, {"text": "table cloth is removed quickly from under the dining implements, the implements will", "x0": 0.21318681318681318, "y0": 0.3123543123543124, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.3333333333333333}, {"text": "remain unmoved. This is best explained in terms of", "x0": 0.14835164835164835, "y0": 0.3278943278943279, "x1": 0.5461538461538461, "y1": 0.3434343434343434}, {"text": "a) second law of motion", "x0": 0.14835164835164835, "y0": 0.3581973581973582, "x1": 0.43956043956043955, "y1": 0.37218337218337216}, {"text": "b) Inertia", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.37373737373737376, "x1": 0.24505494505494504, "y1": 0.3861693861693862}, {"text": "\u00a9) Velocity", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.38927738927738925, "x1": 0.26153846153846155, "y1": 0.4024864024864025}, {"text": "d) third law of motion", "x0": 0.14725274725274726, "y0": 0.4048174048174048, "x1": 0.421978021978022, "y1": 0.41802641802641805}, {"text": "13.", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.43512043512043513, "x1": 0.12967032967032968, "y1": 0.44522144522144524}, {"text": "The unit called the light year is a measure of", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.4358974358974359, "x1": 0.4912087912087912, "y1": 0.4506604506604507}, {"text": "a) light velocity", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.466977466977467, "x1": 0.2956043956043956, "y1": 0.48096348096348096}, {"text": "b) speed", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.48174048174048173, "x1": 0.23626373626373626, "y1": 0.49572649572649574}, {"text": "\u00a9) acceleration", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.49805749805749805, "x1": 0.2846153846153846, "y1": 0.5104895104895105}, {"text": "\u00a9) stellar distance", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.5128205128205128, "x1": 0.3076923076923077, "y1": 0.526029526029526}, {"text": "The first of the early astronomers to suggest a heliocentri\u00e9 method for the universe was", "x0": 0.14285714285714285, "y0": 0.54001554001554, "x1": 0.8142857142857143, "y1": 0.5672105672105672}, {"text": "Aristarchus", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.567987567987568, "x1": 0.27912087912087913, "y1": 0.5866355866355867}, {"text": "b) Plato", "x0": 0.14175824175824175, "y0": 0.5905205905205905, "x1": 0.22857142857142856, "y1": 0.602952602952603}, {"text": "Galileo", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.6068376068376068, "x1": 0.24505494505494504, "y1": 0.616938616938617}, {"text": "d) \u2014 Copemicus", "x0": 0.14175824175824175, "y0": 0.6153846153846154, "x1": 0.27692307692307694, "y1": 0.6410256410256411}, {"text": ". Which of the following was predicted by Friedmann and later verified by Hubble?", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6526806526806527, "x1": 0.7747252747252747, "y1": 0.6728826728826729}, {"text": "a) The Big Bang occurred 13 billion years ago", "x0": 0.13956043956043956, "y0": 0.6837606837606838, "x1": 0.5252747252747253, "y1": 0.7016317016317016}, {"text": "b) The universe is expanding", "x0": 0.13846153846153847, "y0": 0.6993006993006993, "x1": 0.3912087912087912, "y1": 0.7148407148407149}, {"text": "\u00a9) The universe was initially extremely hot", "x0": 0.13846153846153847, "y0": 0.7148407148407149, "x1": 0.4989010989010989, "y1": 0.7311577311577312}, {"text": "Allarge telescope in the Earth's orbit would be able to see further into the universe than", "x0": 0.18461538461538463, "y0": 0.7311577311577312, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.7505827505827506}, {"text": "ever before", "x0": 0.18461538461538463, "y0": 0.7466977466977467, "x1": 0.2725274725274725, "y1": 0.7575757575757576}, {"text": "End of Section I", "x0": 0.4197802197802198, "y0": 0.8562548562548562, "x1": 0.5494505494505495, "y1": 0.8694638694638694}], [{"text": "Name: ..", "x0": 0.08681318681318681, "y0": 0.08313908313908314, "x1": 0.15384615384615385, "y1": 0.09246309246309246}, {"text": "Section I \u2014 Extended Response", "x0": 0.08901098901098901, "y0": 0.0947940947940948, "x1": 0.34615384615384615, "y1": 0.10878010878010878}, {"text": "57 marks", "x0": 0.09010989010989011, "y0": 0.11344211344211344, "x1": 0.16373626373626374, "y1": 0.12432012432012432}, {"text": "\u2018Answer the questions in the spaces provided", "x0": 0.09010989010989011, "y0": 0.12276612276612277, "x1": 0.45164835164835165, "y1": 0.14063714063714064}, {"text": "Mark values are indicated for individual questions", "x0": 0.09010989010989011, "y0": 0.13752913752913754, "x1": 0.5043956043956044, "y1": 0.1554001554001554}, {"text": "Show all relevant working in questions involving calculations", "x0": 0.09230769230769231, "y0": 0.15151515151515152, "x1": 0.5901098901098901, "y1": 0.1717171717171717}, {"text": "Marks", "x0": 0.8098901098901099, "y0": 0.1794871794871795, "x1": 0.8637362637362638, "y1": 0.1895881895881896}, {"text": "Question 16 (2 marks)", "x0": 0.0945054945054945, "y0": 0.20745920745920746, "x1": 0.27362637362637365, "y1": 0.222999222999223}, {"text": "\u2018Two different metallic conductors, A and B, have their variations in current with changes in 2", "x0": 0.0956043956043956, "y0": 0.2261072261072261, "x1": 0.8538461538461538, "y1": 0.2517482517482518}, {"text": "their potential difference, shown in the graph below.", "x0": 0.0967032967032967, "y0": 0.2494172494172494, "x1": 0.4978021978021978, "y1": 0.26961926961926963}, 