 "x1": 0.8395604395604396, "y1": 0.7987567987567987}, {"text": "to operate all of these appliances for one and a half hours?", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.7948717948717948, "x1": 0.5681318681318681, "y1": 0.8166278166278166}, {"text": "ke", "x0": 0.9197802197802197, "y0": 0.8018648018648019, "x1": 0.9351648351648352, "y1": 0.8181818181818182}, {"text": "Lm", "x0": 0.8857142857142857, "y0": 0.8057498057498057, "x1": 0.9175824175824175, "y1": 0.8205128205128205}], [{"text": "Marks", "x0": 0.8208791208791208, "y0": 0.07226107226107226, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.08236208236208237}, {"text": "Question 18 (6 marks)", "x0": 0.1054945054945055, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.2857142857142857, "y1": 0.10101010101010101}, {"text": "For the circuit diagram below, determine", "x0": 0.1043956043956044, "y0": 0.11888111888111888, "x1": 0.4197802197802198, "y1": 0.13286713286713286}, {"text": "A 36V D", "x0": 0.21978021978021978, "y0": 0.14607614607614608, "x1": 0.6417582417582418, "y1": 0.16317016317016317}, {"text": "102", "x0": 0.6285714285714286, "y0": 0.22766122766122765, "x1": 0.6604395604395604, "y1": 0.236985236985237}, {"text": "c", "x0": 0.6241758241758242, "y0": 0.2999222999222999, "x1": 0.6351648351648351, "y1": 0.30924630924630925}, {"text": "a) the current flowing through the 4 Q resistor 2", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.432012432012432, "x1": 0.8648351648351649, "y1": 0.445998445998446}, {"text": "b) 1", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.5866355866355867, "x1": 0.8648351648351649, "y1": 0.6006216006216006}, {"text": "\u00b0 2", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.6923076923076923, "x1": 0.8670329670329671, "y1": 0.7070707070707071}, {"text": "1", "x0": 0.8615384615384616, "y0": 0.8010878010878011, "x1": 0.8681318681318682, "y1": 0.8104118104118104}], [{"text": "Marks", "x0": 0.8131868131868132, "y0": 0.057498057498057496, "x1": 0.8670329670329671, "y1": 0.0675990675990676}, {"text": "Question 19 (6 marks)", "x0": 0.0956043956043956, "y0": 0.07614607614607614, "x1": 0.27802197802197803, "y1": 0.09013209013209013}, {"text": "For this question refer to the incomplete Hertzsprung-Russell diagram shown below", "x0": 0.0956043956043956, "y0": 0.09557109557109557, "x1": 0.7428571428571429, "y1": 0.11421911421911422}, {"text": "Absolute Magnitude", "x0": 0.11758241758241758, "y0": 0.18414918414918416, "x1": 0.13406593406593406, "y1": 0.28205128205128205}, {"text": "Spectral Class", "x0": 0.2802197802197802, "y0": 0.3278943278943279, "x1": 0.3813186813186813, "y1": 0.33877233877233875}, {"text": "a) Suggest two (2) alternative labels for the horizontal axis 2", "x0": 0.1021978021978022, "y0": 0.34965034965034963, "x1": 0.8626373626373627, "y1": 0.36985236985236986}, {"text": "\u00a9) Hertzsprung-Russell diagram above, clearly show the positions of", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.48717948717948717, "x1": 0.7120879120879121, "y1": 0.5058275058275058}, {"text": "i) the main sequence One 1", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.5135975135975136, "x1": 0.865934065934066, "y1": 0.5369075369075369}, {"text": "ii) aed giant eh", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.533022533022533, "x1": 0.5307692307692308, "y1": 0.5524475524475524}, {"text": "iii) a white dwarf b etm. 1", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.5485625485625486, "x1": 0.8670329670329671, "y1": 0.5773115773115773}, {"text": "Question 20 (2 marks)", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.6013986013986014, "x1": 0.29120879120879123, "y1": 0.6153846153846154}, {"text": "Describe the composition of the solar wind.", "x0": 0.10989010989010989, "y0": 0.6301476301476302, "x1": 0.4461538461538462, "y1": 0.6441336441336442}], [{"text": "Question 21 (4 marks)", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.08702408702408702, "x1": 0.2879120879120879, "y1": 0.10023310023310024}, {"text": "The \"Big Bang\" Theory is described in the context of the following statement:", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.11732711732711733, "x1": 0.7087912087912088, "y1": 0.13053613053613053}, {"text": "Space-time and matter came into existence spontaneously, from absolutely nothing. This", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.1655011655011655, "x1": 0.8373626373626374, "y1": 0.1794871794871795}, {"text": "happened about 14 thousand million years ago (give or take a few thousand million years).", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.18104118104118105, "x1": 0.8351648351648352, "y1": 0.19502719502719504}, {"text": "The universe was initially a tiny entity, -which immediately began to expand, and which has", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.1888111888111888, "x1": 0.8373626373626374, "y1": 0.21522921522921523}, {"text": "been expanding ever since, *", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.21367521367521367, "x1": 0.32857142857142857, "y1": 0.22688422688422688}, {"text": "The\u2019 question was not an explosion into a void but the swelling or stretching of space itself.", "x0": 0.10329670329670329, "y0": 0.236985236985237, "x1": 0.8373626373626374, "y1": 0.26262626262626265}, {"text": "The early, small, univers\u00e9 was extremely hot, an opaque: soup of particles and photons,", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.25874125874125875, "x1": 0.8362637362637363, "y1": 0.27350427350427353}, {"text": "constantly interacting. As the universe expanded, it cooled.", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.27505827505827507, "x1": 0.5615384615384615, "y1": 0.289044289044289}, {"text": "At the age of about 300 000 years, the universe was cool enough for protons and electrons to", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.3061383061383061, "x1": 0.8384615384615385, "y1": 0.3201243201243201}, {"text": "form stable atoms. Matter and radiation were and the universe became", "x0": 0.1043956043956044, "y0": 0.32167832167832167, "x1": 0.8384615384615385, "y1": 0.3356643356643357}, {"text": "transparent, with photons free to distances. Small irregularities in the composition", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.3372183372183372, "x1": 0.8384615384615385, "y1": 0.35120435120435123}, {"text": "of the early universe formed the 'seeds' of the structures that evolved into the early galaxies.", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.3504273504273504, "x1": 0.8131868131868132, "y1": 0.3667443667443667}, {"text": "\u2018There are a great many pieces of observational \u00e9vidence supporting the 'Big Bang\u2019 Theory", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.40093240093240096, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.4149184149184149}, {"text": "but four (4) of them are considered fundamental.", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.4087024087024087, "x1": 0.4835164835164835, "y1": 0.43512043512043513}, {"text": "Of these four, list TWO fundamental observations and for each, explain how it supported", "x0": 0.1043956043956044, "y0": 0.439005439005439, "x1": 0.7967032967032966, "y1": 0.4654234654234654}, {"text": "4", "x0": 0.8593406593406593, "y0": 0.44755244755244755, "x1": 0.8681318681318682, "y1": 0.45765345765345766}, {"text": "the 'Big Bang\u2019 Theory.", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.46386946386946387, "x1": 0.27802197802197803, "y1": 0.47707847707847706}], [{"text": "Question 22 (5 marks)", "x0": 0.1010989010989011, "y0": 0.07925407925407925, "x1": 0.2813186813186813, "y1": 0.09246309246309246}, {"text": "a) Explain the electrical implications that follow if a short circuit should arise within an 3", "x0": 0.1010989010989011, "y0": 0.10567210567210568, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.12354312354312354}, {"text": "fom path & nat bud han", "x0": 0.2230769230769231, "y0": 0.11965811965811966, "x1": 0.7725274725274726, "y1": 0.16317016317016317}, {"text": "b) Name a device that could protect us against a dangerous short circuit.", "x0": 0.1043956043956044, "y0": 0.28438228438228436, "x1": 0.676923076923077, "y1": 0.31157731157731156}, {"text": "Explain exactly how this device operates. 5 fig rs", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.29526029526029524, "x1": 0.5868131868131868, "y1": 0.32323232323232326}, {"text": "Question 23 (3 marks)", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.4467754467754468, "x1": 0.289010989010989, "y1": 0.45998445998445997}, {"text": "In the spaces below, sketch the magnetic field around the following:", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.4755244755244755, "x1": 0.6329670329670329, "y1": 0.49184149184149184}, {"text": "a) Along, straight wire .", "x0": 0.10989010989010989, "y0": 0.5081585081585082, "x1": 0.5054945054945055, "y1": 0.5221445221445221}, {"text": "nan ~ of", "x0": 0.13736263736263737, "y0": 0.5446775446775447, "x1": 0.43736263736263736, "y1": 0.6076146076146076}, {"text": "2", "x0": 0.865934065934066, "y0": 0.7062937062937062, "x1": 0.8747252747252747, "y1": 0.7156177156177156}], [{"text": "Marks", "x0": 0.8241758241758241, "y0": 0.0707070707070707, "x1": 0.8769230769230769, "y1": 0.08003108003108003}, {"text": "Question 24 (2 marks)", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.08624708624708624, "x1": 0.2879120879120879, "y1": 0.09945609945609946}, {"text": "Your task is to design the strongest electromagnet that you can.", "x0": 0.10659340659340659, "y0": 0.11732711732711733, "x1": 0.5945054945054945, "y1": 0.12975912975912976}, {"text": "a) List the design features that you would include. 2", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.14840714840714841, "x1": 0.8648351648351649, "y1": 0.16161616161616163}, {"text": "Question 25 (3 marks)", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.2867132867132867, "x1": 0.29010989010989013, "y1": 0.29914529914529914}, {"text": "In each of the three diagrams below, draw the continuation of all light rays using a ruler.", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.30924630924630925, "x1": 0.789010989010989, "y1": 0.3341103341103341}, {"text": "Label any significant angles. Note that the focal length of the concave mirror is 5 cm. Precise angles", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.3317793317793318, "x1": 0.8791208791208791, "y1": 0.34498834498834496}, {"text": "will not be measured in the marking of this question, so you do not have to use a protractor.", "x0": 0.1087912087912088, "y0": 0.34032634032634035, "x1": 0.81428571