 travelling in air is about to enter a block of perspex of Refractive Index", "x0": 0.11318681318681319, "y0": 0.5811965811965812, "x1": 0.8395604395604396, "y1": 0.5998445998445998}, {"text": "1.4 at an angle to the surface of 60\u00b0.", "x0": 0.11538461538461539, "y0": 0.5998445998445998, "x1": 0.3923076923076923, "y1": 0.6153846153846154}, {"text": "8) the number of degrees that the wave will deviate through as it enters the glass. 3", "x0": 0.11428571428571428, "y0": 0.627039627039627, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.6472416472416472}], [{"text": "Marks", "x0": 0.8208791208791208, "y0": 0.061383061383061384, "x1": 0.8747252747252747, "y1": 0.0707070707070707}, {"text": "32 (2 marks)", "x0": 0.18021978021978022, "y0": 0.07847707847707848, "x1": 0.2835164835164835, "y1": 0.09090909090909091}, {"text": "Infra Red", "x0": 0.6626373626373626, "y0": 0.09324009324009325, "x1": 0.7351648351648352, "y1": 0.10334110334110334}, {"text": "Gamma Light Microwaves", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.10023310023310024, "x1": 0.7461538461538462, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "X Rays Television", "x0": 0.2, "y0": 0.12432012432012432, "x1": 0.7395604395604396, "y1": 0.1383061383061383}, {"text": "Ultra Violet Radio", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.13986013986013987, "x1": 0.721978021978022, "y1": 0.15151515151515152}, {"text": "State two reasons why all of the above types of radiation gre similar. 2", "x0": 0.1043956043956044, "y0": 0.16394716394716394, "x1": 0.8626373626373627, "y1": 0.19036519036519037}, {"text": "wee oP inv. \u20ac vr 341 0 .", "x0": 0.16593406593406593, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.9021978021978022, "y1": 0.21056721056721056}, {"text": "arnt", "x0": 0.6263736263736264, "y0": 0.1926961926961927, "x1": 0.710989010989011, "y1": 0.22688422688422688}, {"text": "olen b", "x0": 0.37252747252747254, "y0": 0.21445221445221446, "x1": 0.9120879120879121, "y1": 0.236985236985237}, {"text": "a aed", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.22921522921522922, "